<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44575" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔξενος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔξεινος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>kind to
				strangers, hospitable</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρῶνας
				εὐ. δόμων</span>
			<i>the guest</i>-chambers, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				712
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμὴν εὐξεινότατος ναύταις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					157
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). 
				Ep.
			
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐϋξείνως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.963
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				1179
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόντος εὔ</span>. <i>the Euxine</i>,
			now <i>the Black Sea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.6
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				125
			</span></i> (lyr., codd., sed leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀξείνου</span>); and so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ</span>.
			(leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξ-</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> οἶδμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HF</u>
					410
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. πέλαγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					4.49
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Εὔξεινος</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.1.5
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξενος</span>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔξεινος</span> is a euphemism, 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐμενίδες</span>
			.</div>
